 "reading": {
  "main": "the cursor rides the SDK internal slot tracker to the live head (122) even when the USER subscription is silent \u2014 so the proposed \"cursor only advances on delivered payloads\" is NOT what main does today; at age-out (floor 130) the server refuses 122 with OUT_OF_RANGE.",
  "pr114": "the payload-only cursor stops at the newest DELIVERED payload (91) \u2014 it does NOT ride the tracker \u2014 but at the same age-out it is refused too (91 < 130), and it would be refused EARLIER than main (91 lags 122). The reservation holds: payload-only does not survive age-out either.",
  "default_options": "OUT_OF_RANGE is a transient error for a default-configured consumer (intra_slot_updates=false): 0 consumer errors, silent 5 s retry loop, 2+ refused attempts inside 12 s. The stall is invisible to the application.",
  "intra_slot_updates": "with intra_slot_updates=true the SDK surfaces OUT_OF_RANGE as a terminal stream error (1 consumer error) \u2014 the SDK already owns the switch that makes the stall visible; it is off by default.",
  "held_window": "the false-positive guard: main serves from 122 and loses 92..121 EVEN IN-WINDOW (the #115 skip in quiet form); PR #114 recovers 91..122 with zero loss."
 },
 "limits": "mock geyser; window model = a single floor below which OUT_OF_RANGE is returned (real LaserStream retention semantics approximated, not measured against real infrastructure); Rust SDK only; PR #114 applied to the 2.0.0 crate, not a live branch checkout."
